The attached image (Fig. 1) illustrates the dendrimer-like structure of phytoglycogen (PG) and its chemical modifications. The top image shows native phytoglycogen (PG). The middle image shows phytoglycogen octenyl succinate (PG-OS), where an octenyl succinate group introduces a negative charge. The bottom image displays PG-OS-CHPTAC, also termed Nano-11, which incorporates a positively charged quaternary ammonium group. These schematics, paired with the associated chemical formulas, demonstrate the chemical engineering used to create Nano-11, a positively charged nanoparticle designed for effective antigen adsorption and adjuvant function.